fact WorkItem(id: "WI-317", description: some(value: "Inferred-effects model for operations: derive an op effect row from its body instead of requiring a declaration. WI-314 built the operation-boundary masking engine (kb/region.rs op_boundary_effects) and left the boundary as a CHECKED seam (actual subset-of declared). This WI extends that seam to INFERENCE: when an op opts in (an explicit effects-Inferred marker, or a WI-307 effects-? row-variable on a bodied op -- NOT bare-absent, which today means open/pure), the typer SETS the op effect row to the masked/re-keyed row that op_boundary_effects already computes, and writes it back to OperationInfo.effects so call sites (typing.rs call-effect accrual ~line 2006) propagate it. Effect: Cell.new-style allocation becomes non-viral WITHOUT per-op declarations -- make(n) -> Cell = Cell.new(n) carries an INFERRED Modify[result] (CSE-safe: present in the row callers/CSE see) without the author writing it, while allocate-and-discard ops infer the empty row. PIECES BEYOND WI-314 ENGINE: (a) write the computed row back into OperationInfo so callers read the inferred row (checked model needs no write-back -- the declaration IS the row); (b) a monotone fixpoint over the finite effect-label set for recursive ops (infer chain row from chain row), trivial/absent for non-recursive ops; (c) the effects-Inferred trigger kept DISTINCT from absent (=open/pure today), coordinated with WI-307 row-variable semantics. Inferring an op row from its body IS effect propagation = WI-307 phase 4/5; WI-314 masking makes the inferred row CORRECT (drops Modify on non-escaping locals). The checked->inferred transform is clean because both models consume the same masked row. ACCEPTANCE: an op with the inference trigger whose body allocates and returns a cell type-checks with no written effect AND its callers see the inferred Modify[result]; recursive allocating ops converge via the fixpoint; full cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-314", "WI-307"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
